  </div>
</section>

{# SECTION 9 — COST — UX: accordion with + circle, FE: focus-visible, Motion: rotate 45deg #}
<section class="bg-white py-[var(--linoxa-section)]">
  <div class="container-wx">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-5">
        <h2 class="linoxa-h2 text-[#111111]">What Affects the Cost of 3D Rendering?</h2>
        <p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[#525252]">3D rendering fees are determined by the complexity and scope of the project — not by a fixed per-image rate. The following seven factors directly affect the cost of your Woodex 3D Studio™ commission.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 linoxa-card bg-[#fcf2e8] p-6 border-[#0f1e36]/10">
          <p class="text-[13px] font-medium leading-[1.6] text-[#111]">Woodex 3D Studio™ provides a detailed, confirmed quotation based on your drawings, brief and output requirements — within one business day of receiving your project brief. Submit your brief today and receive a confirmed fee before any work begins.</p>
          <a href="#commission" class="linoxa-btn mt-6"><span>Submit Your 3D Brief</span><span class="arrow"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7">
        <div class="space-y-3" id="cost-accordion">
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-[#f8f8f8]" open><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 1: Render Type — Still, Animation or Virtual Tour <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-white border border-black/10 flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Still renders — individual photorealistic images at specific camera angles — are the simplest and most affordable output type. Animated walkthroughs require significantly more modelling, rendering time and post-production than still images. 360° virtual tours require specialized rendering and hosting setup. Each output type carries a different production cost, reflected in the quotation.</p></details>
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-white"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 2: Number of Images or Scenes <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-[#f8f8f8] flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">The total number of camera angles, rooms or scenes required directly determines the total project cost. A single reception area render costs less than a complete floor visualization covering open-plan workstations, meeting rooms, a boardroom, a reception and breakout zones. Volume discounts apply on larger commissions — confirmed in the quotation.</p></details>
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-[#f8f8f8]"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 3: Scene Complexity <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-white border border-black/10 flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">A simple room with standard furniture and flat ceilings renders faster and costs less than a complex scene with curved ceilings, custom joinery, detailed material finishes, multiple light sources and densely furnished spaces. The geometric complexity of the scene is one of the primary drivers of modelling and rendering time.</p></details>
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-white"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 4: Level of Detail and Realism <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-[#f8f8f8] flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Photorealistic output requires significantly more modelling time, higher-quality material libraries and longer rendering computation than presentation-quality output. The level of realism specified — standard presentation or photorealistic — affects both production time and cost.</p></details>
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-[#f8f8f8]"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 5: Material and Furniture Sourcing <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-white border border-black/10 flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Where material textures, finish samples or furniture models need to be sourced, modelled or licensed for the project — rather than drawn from the studio's existing library — this adds to the production time and cost. Providing material samples, product files or reference images at the brief stage reduces this variable significantly.</p></details>
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-white"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 6: Revision Rounds Required <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-[#f8f8f8] flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Each quotation includes a standard number of revision rounds — typically two. Additional revisions beyond the agreed scope are charged at a confirmed per-revision rate. Providing a clear, complete brief and consolidated feedback at each review stage minimizes revision requirements and keeps the project on schedule.</p></details>
          <details class="linoxa-card p-6 bg-[#f8f8f8]"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[14px] text-[#111]">Factor 7: Turnaround Time — Rush Fee <span class="acc-icon w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-white border border-black/10 flex items-center justify-center text-[14px] transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Standard turnaround timelines are confirmed at the quotation stage based on current studio capacity. Projects requiring expedited delivery — where the standard timeline must be compressed to meet a pitch deadline, presentation date or marketing launch — carry a rush fee that is confirmed before work begins.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# SECTION 10 — WHY CHOOSE — Creative: SVG icons, UX: dark card contrast 15.2:1, Motion: hover border #}
<section class="bg-[#f8f8f8] py-[var(--linoxa-section)]">
  <div class="container-wx">
    <div class="text-center max-w-[720px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="linoxa-h2 text-[#111111]">Why Choose Woodex 3D Studio™?</h2>
      <p class="linoxa-sub mt-4 text-[#525252]">Six reasons architects, developers and designers commission Woodex as their Pakistan rendering partner — from photorealistic standard to integrated workflow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
      <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-4"><div class="linoxa-card p-7 bg-white h-full"><div class="linoxa-icon bg-[#fcf2e8]"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0f1e36" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold mt-5 text-[#111]">Photorealistic Output Standard</h3><p class="linoxa-sub mt-3 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Woodex 3D Studio™ produces photorealistic renders — not presentation-quality approximations. Every scene is modelled accurately from the provided drawings, rendered with physically correct lighting and materials and delivered at high resolution suitable for large-format printing and broadcast-quality media.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-4"><div class="linoxa-card p-7 bg-white h-full"><div class="linoxa-icon bg-[#f8f8f8]"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="7" width="20" height="14"/><path d="M16 7V5a2 2 0 00-2-2h-4a2 2 0 00-2 2v2"/></svg></div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold mt-5 text-[#111]">Interior and Exterior Capability</h3><p class="linoxa-sub mt-3 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">The studio produces visualization for interior spaces — offices, residences, retail environments, healthcare facilities and hospitality projects — and architectural exteriors — building facades, site developments, street-level perspectives and aerial views. Both capabilities are available within the same studio, from the same team.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-4"><div class="linoxa-card p-7 bg-white h-full"><div class="linoxa-icon bg-[#fcf2e8]"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0f1e36" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"/></svg></div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold mt-5 text-[#111]">Fast Turnaround — Confirmed at Quotation</h3><p class="linoxa-sub mt-3 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">Every Woodex 3D Studio™ quotation includes a confirmed turnaround timeline — not an estimate. The delivery date is agreed before work begins and respected throughout the project. For urgent commissions, rush delivery is available at a confirmed premium — also agreed before work starts.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-4"><div class="linoxa-card p-7 bg-white h-full"><div class="linoxa-icon bg-[#f8f8f8]"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="20" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 8v-2M12 18v-2M8 12H6M18 12h-2"/></svg></div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold mt-5 text-[#111]">Full Range — Still, Animation and Virtual Tour</h3><p class="linoxa-sub mt-3 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">The studio produces every format of visualization output — photorealistic still renders, animated walkthroughs, 360° virtual tours and sciography studies — under one roof. You do not need to source multiple studios for different output types.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-4"><div class="linoxa-card-dark p-7 bg-[#0f1e36] h-full hover:bg-[#121f3a] transition"><div class="linoxa-icon bg-white/10"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="white" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0110 0v4"/></svg></div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold mt-5 text-white">Available Independently — No Fit-Out Required</h3><p class="linoxa-sub mt-3 text-[13px] text-white/70">External architects, developers, designers and marketing agencies can commission Woodex 3D Studio™ directly — independently of any interior design, fit-out or furniture service from Woodex Interior. The studio is a standalone professional service available to the entire design and property industry.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-4"><div class="linoxa-card p-7 bg-white h-full"><div class="linoxa-icon bg-[#fcf2e8]"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0f1e36" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg></div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold mt-5 text-[#111]">Integrated With Woodex Interior Projects</h3><p class="linoxa-sub mt-3 text-[13px] text-[#525252]">For clients who commission interior design or turnkey delivery through Woodex Interior, 3D visualization is produced by the same studio — fully integrated with the design process. The 3D team works directly from the design team's drawings and material schedules — with no file translation, no brief repetition and no quality gap between the design and the render.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

